<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adalrich, Duke of Alsace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">?–c. 690</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Eticho</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adalrich, also called Eticho, was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> in the later 7th century and founder of the Etichonid family. A powerful noble in Merovingian politics, he endowed monasteries in Alsace. His daughter Odile founded the convent of Hohenburg on what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mont-sainte-odile">Mont Sainte-Odile</a> and became the patron saint of Alsace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adalrich-duke-of-alsace.jpg" alt="Adalrich, Duke of Alsace" width="320" height="531" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Pixelk at French Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 2.0 fr · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adalric.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
